  "title": "Kebra Nagast",
  "summary": "The Kebra Nagast is an Ethiopian text that scholars place in the 1300s; Ethiopian belief holds it was found in Constantinople in the third century. World History Encyclopedia says it was written to legitimise the dynasty of Yekuno Amlak against the Zagwe, though scholars disagree on who wrote it and when.",
